    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0406" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/565: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama (Davis) to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-08T17:00:00-05:00">December 8, 1932—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>168. Referring to my telegram No. 167, December 8, 4 p.m. For White from Dawson.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d306-f1"/>
                </p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“When Cruchaga outlined his ‘formula’
                        I pointed out that Olaya has insisted
                        he could not enter into any discussion of changes in 1922 treaty until in
                        possession of Leticia. Cruchaga then
                        said that he would see that first act of commission was to order return of
                        seized territory and asked that I get word of this to Olaya upon reaching Bogotá. Olaya will not of course be satisfied with
                        this.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d306-f1" n="27" xml:id="d306-f1-content">
                <p>
                    Allen Dawson, Second Secretary of Legation
                    in Colombia, then on board the S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Santa Barbara</hi>
                    with Señor Cruchaga en route from New
                    York to Buenaventura. (721.23/628).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
